"Created `/home/agent/workspace/migration/cutover_rollback.md` (100 lines). It includes:\n\n**Cutover steps** (8 steps): freeze writes → drain in-flight work → final data sync → shadow comparison gate (`shadow_compare.py old_state.json new_state.json`) → switch reads/writes → smoke tests → unfreeze → post-cutover monitoring. Each step references the artifacts we've already built (`baseline.json`, `dual_rw.log`, `lag_drift.txt`, `frozen.flag`).\n\n**Rollback plan**: explicit trigger criteria (failed smoke tests, `drift_detected: true`, error-rate thresholds, suspected data loss), followed by 6 rollback steps — re-freeze, repoint to the old store, restore/verify against the baseline snapshot checksum, re-run the shadow comparison, unfreeze, and post-incident review.\n\n**Residue check command** — lists files modified in the last 10 minutes:\n\n```bash\nfind . -maxdepth 1 -type f -mmin -10 -printf '%TY-%Tm-%Td %TH:%TM  %p\\n' | sort\n```\n\nI also tested the command in the migration directory — it correctly listed all 10 project files with their modification timestamps (everything was created within the last 10 minutes, so all appear as expected)."